      "problem": "Factor $x^2 + 12x + 36.$",
      "worked_solution": "The \"square of a sum\" formula states that\n\n$$\nx^2 + {\\color{red}{2}}{\\color{blue}{a}} x + a^2 =  (x+{\\color{blue}{a}})^2 .\n$$\n\nWe will use this formula to factor the given trinomial. Our trinomial is\n\n$$\nx^2 + 12x + 36.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the constant term as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+12x+{6}^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we factor a $2$ out of the linear term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 6x+{6}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the trinomial using the square of sum formula with ${\\color{blue}{a}} = {\\color{blue}{6}}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+6)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
